# LocalVault Web Frontend Environment Configuration

# --- Local Development ---
# In local development, leaving these commented or pointing to localhost proxies /api/v1 to port 8000.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
# BACKEND_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# --- Vercel Production Deployment ---
# REQUIRED: Set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL in your Vercel Project Settings (Settings -> Environment Variables).
# This points client-side browser requests to your laptop's FastAPI backend over HTTPS.
# IMPORTANT:
# 1. Must use HTTPS (e.g. Cloudflare Tunnel or Tailscale Funnel). Modern browsers block unencrypted HTTP.
# 2. Do NOT use localhost/127.0.0.1 (in browser code, localhost resolves to the client's device, not your laptop).
#
# Examples:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://vault-api.yourdomain.com/api/v1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://random-subdomain.trycloudflare.com/api/v1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://laptop-name.tailscale.net/api/v1
